    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d96-a1">

                <pb facs="0259" n="163" xml:id="pg163"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 88.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wilson to Mr.
                            Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Department of Agriculture</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington, D. C.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1898-01-11"><hi rendition="#italic">January
                                11, 1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose for your
                    information copy of a translation from a Belgian paper, which is forwarded to us
                    by Messrs. Swift &amp; Co., of Chicago. Will you kindly inform me if your
                    Department has any information of the proposed regulations respecting the
                    importation of salted meats into Belgium, and if you have not received such
                    information, will you please make inquiry of the American minister to that
                    country as to whether such regulations have been made or are contemplated.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James Wilson</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
